{% comment %}
  Shared "Your Progress" desktop stepper (Figma node/export "Desktop
  Progress") — originally built inline in kal-booking-flow-step-concern-select.liquid
  for that step alone, extracted here once Doctor Select needed the exact
  same list with a different current step, so the 5 step names/order live
  in exactly one place instead of drifting between per-step copies.

  Accepts:
  - current_step: {Number} 1-based, which step is "in progress" right
    now. Steps before it render as completed (checkmark, filled
    dark-green circle); the one immediately after it renders as "Up
    next" (the lighter tan-bordered --next look); every step after that
    renders plain, with no state text at all — matching the original
    concern-select export's own greying-out of later, not-yet-relevant
    steps.
  - step_names: {String} optional, pipe-separated (e.g.
    'Choose therapy|Personal details') — defaults to the 5-step
    consultation flow's own names if omitted, so every existing caller
    keeps working unchanged. Lets shorter flows (the 2-step therapy
    flow) reuse this exact same stepper instead of a parallel copy.

  Usage:
  {% render 'kal-booking-flow-step-progress', current_step: 2 %}
  {% render 'kal-booking-flow-step-progress', current_step: 1, step_names: 'Choose therapy|Personal details' %}

  Still uses the .kal-concern-select__* class names from that first
  build (stepper/stepper-step/stepper-number/etc., and the outer
  .kal-concern-select__progress) rather than a step-agnostic rename —
  reused as-is on Doctor Select's left column too, same as this flow's
  other shared pieces (see kal-booking-flow-step-header.liquid's own
  comment on why one CSS definition beats duplicating it per step).
{% endcomment %}

{%- liquid
  assign step_names_string = step_names | default: 'Health concerns|Mode & doctor|Date & time|Patient Details|Review & payment'
  assign step_names = step_names_string | split: '|'
  assign next_step = current_step | plus: 1
-%}

<div class="kal-concern-select__progress">
  <p class="kal-concern-select__info-label">Your Progress</p>
  <ol class="kal-concern-select__stepper">
    {%- for step_name in step_names -%}
      {%- assign step_index = forloop.index -%}
      {%- assign is_last = forloop.last -%}
      {%- if step_index < current_step -%}
        {%- assign state_modifier = ' kal-concern-select__stepper-step--completed' -%}
        {%- assign state_text = 'Completed' -%}
      {%- elsif step_index == current_step -%}
        {%- assign state_modifier = ' kal-concern-select__stepper-step--current' -%}
        {%- assign state_text = 'In progress' -%}
      {%- elsif step_index == next_step -%}
        {%- assign state_modifier = ' kal-concern-select__stepper-step--next' -%}
        {%- assign state_text = 'Up next' -%}
      {%- else -%}
        {%- assign state_modifier = '' -%}
        {%- assign state_text = '' -%}
      {%- endif -%}
      <li class="kal-concern-select__stepper-step{{ state_modifier }}">
        <div class="kal-concern-select__stepper-row">
          <span class="kal-concern-select__stepper-number">
            {%- if step_index < current_step -%}
              {%- render 'kal-booking-icons', icon_name: 'check' -%}
            {%- else -%}
              {{ step_index }}
            {%- endif -%}
          </span>
          <span class="kal-concern-select__stepper-text">
            <span class="kal-concern-select__stepper-label">{{ step_name }}</span>
            {%- if state_text != '' -%}
              <span class="kal-concern-select__stepper-state">{{ state_text }}</span>
            {%- endif -%}
          </span>
        </div>
        {%- unless is_last -%}
          <span class="kal-concern-select__stepper-divider" aria-hidden="true"></span>
        {%- endunless -%}
      </li>
    {%- endfor -%}
  </ol>
</div>
